        "original_id": "98f9378d-75e5-557e-ac09-cbf3ab22759f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Kanin, Ring Lardner Jr., Katharine Hepburn, Spencer Tracy\n- Works: Woman of the Year, When I Grow Up\n- Awards: Academy Award\n- Topics: Hollywood blacklist, Red Scare\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Kanin was born on February 1, 1910, and Ring Lardner Jr. was born on August 19, 1915.\n- In 1942, Michael Kanin shared an Academy Award with Ring Lardner Jr. for writing the Katharine Hepburn and Spencer Tracy film comedy Woman of the Year.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was an American journalist and screenwriter who was blacklisted by Hollywood movie studios during the Red Scare of the late 1940s and 1950s.\n- In 1951, When I Grow Up was released as an American drama film written and directed by Michael Kanin.\n- Michael Kanin died on March 12, 1993, and Ring Lardner Jr. died on October 31, 2000.",
